ios: mobile layout (area canvases, a full-screen viewport, HUD API)

For the mobile HUD (ios/web/host): in game, the viewport, minimap, side panel and chat can each draw into their own
canvas, placed and scaled by the host page (setSurfaceLayout). The classic single-canvas layout stays the default
(no layout set) and is unchanged.

- PixMap can blit into another canvas (retarget, `own`: draws at that canvas's origin).
- The 3D viewport can be any size from 512x334 up (Pix3D clipping, World.resetVisCalc and areaGame follow it). It
  lives on its own island of the virtual coordinate space (x 1024+), so it never overlaps the minimap, tabs, side
  panel or chat, which keep their classic virtual rects and every hit test written for them. Only the viewport's own
  "4, 4, 512, 334" sites take the new rect.
- The host says how much of the viewport its HUD covers (setViewportInsets): the main modal is centred in the rest
  (one that does not fit starts at its left edge and runs on under the HUD on the right, never into the left inset
  with the notch), the main overlay keeps its right edge on it (overlay content is right-aligned), world menus stay
  inside it when they fit, and the tooltip, split private chat, system update timer, multizone icon (with the
  overlay) and "Connection lost" / "Loading" texts stay inside it.
- Input: every surface is bound to the same pointer handlers as the canvas and maps its CSS box onto its virtual
  rect (frozen per touch, with pointer capture). A drag that leaves its surface never clicks or hovers whatever lies
  at those coordinates in another area, and a touch whose surface was hidden under it ends without a click.
  cancelPointer() / cancelPointerOn() end a gesture when the host hides a surface under a finger.
- Menus: the "moved away from the menu" close test includes the point the menu was opened at, and a long-press
  release picks an option only after the finger slid to it (the menu, kept on screen or clear of the HUD, can open
  with an option such as Cancel under a resting finger; in classic that happened at the viewport's bottom edge).
- In the mobile layout a tap on the compass faces north, as in later clients.
- HUD API: tapAt (host controls click like a tap there: the tab column and chat mode buttons tap the classic tabs and
  buttons), hudState (tab, tab availability, flashing tab, modals, chat state, chat modes, run, reconnecting),
  hudChatLines (the chatbox's newest lines with its filters, for the compact chat) and hudSetRun (the Player controls
  Walk / Run buttons; refused while a window is open, because their script closes it). `reconnecting` is set while
  lostCon logs in again (ingame is false meanwhile).

